    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0735" n="727" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg727"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9111/642: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-17T09:00:00+03:25">January 17, 1938—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Department’s 62, December 23, 7 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d577-f1"/> In
                    conversation with the Prime Minister<anchor n="3" xml:id="d577-f2"/> yesterday
                    he assured me that he was making every effort to have the Legation in Washington
                    reopened.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
